[{"answer":"So, welcome to your introductory geography lecture.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/1.mp3"},{"answer":"We'll begin with some basics.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/2.mp3"},{"answer":"Firstly, what do we learn by studying geography?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/3.mp3"},{"answer":"Well, we learn a great deal about all the processes","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/4.mp3"},{"answer":"that have affected and that continue to affect the earth's surface.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/5.mp3"},{"answer":"But we learn far more than that,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/6.mp3"},{"answer":"because studying geography also informs us about the different kinds of relationships","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/7.mp3"},{"answer":"that develop between a particular environment and the people that live there.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/8.mp3"},{"answer":"Okay.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/9.mp3"},{"answer":"We like to think of geography as having two main branches.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/10.mp3"},{"answer":"There's the study of the nature of our planet -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/11.mp3"},{"answer":"its physical features, what it actually looks like -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/12.mp3"},{"answer":"and then there's the study of the ways in which we choose to live","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/13.mp3"},{"answer":"and of the impact of those on our planet.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/14.mp3"},{"answer":"Our current use of carbon fuels is a good example of that.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/15.mp3"},{"answer":"But there are more specific study areas to consider too,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/16.mp3"},{"answer":"and we'll be looking at each of these in turn throughout this semester.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/17.mp3"},{"answer":"These include bio-physical geography,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/18.mp3"},{"answer":"by which I mean the study of the natural environment and all its living things.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/19.mp3"},{"answer":"Then there's topography -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/20.mp3"},{"answer":"that looks at the shapes of the land and oceans.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/21.mp3"},{"answer":"There's the study of political geography and social geography too, of course,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/22.mp3"},{"answer":"which is the study of communities of people.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/23.mp3"},{"answer":"We have economic geography -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/24.mp3"},{"answer":"in which we examine all kinds of resource and their use - agriculture, for example.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/25.mp3"},{"answer":"Next comes historical geography -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/26.mp3"},{"answer":"the understanding of how people and their environments","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/27.mp3"},{"answer":"and the ways they interact have changed over a period of time -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/28.mp3"},{"answer":"and urban geography,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/29.mp3"},{"answer":"an aspect I'm particularly interested in,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/30.mp3"},{"answer":"which takes as its focus: the location of cities,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/31.mp3"},{"answer":"the services that those cities provide.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/32.mp3"},{"answer":"and migration of people to and from such cities.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/33.mp3"},{"answer":"And lastly, we have cartography.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/34.mp3"},{"answer":"That's the art and science of map-making.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/35.mp3"},{"answer":"You'll be doing a lot of that!","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/36.mp3"},{"answer":"So, to summarise before we continue,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/37.mp3"},{"answer":"we now have our key answer...","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/38.mp3"},{"answer":"studying this subject is important","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/39.mp3"},{"answer":"because without geographical knowledge, we would know very little about our surroundings","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/40.mp3"},{"answer":"and we wouldn't be able to identify all the problems that relate to them.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/41.mp3"},{"answer":"So, by definition, we wouldn't be in an informed position to work out how to solve any of them.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/42.mp3"},{"answer":"Okay, now for some practicalities.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/43.mp3"},{"answer":"What do geographers actually do?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/44.mp3"},{"answer":"Well, we collect data to begin with!","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/45.mp3"},{"answer":"You'll be doing a lot of that on your first field trip!","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/46.mp3"},{"answer":"How do we do this?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/47.mp3"},{"answer":"There are several means.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/48.mp3"},{"answer":"We might, for example, conduct a census -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/49.mp3"},{"answer":"count a population in a given area perhaps.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/50.mp3"},{"answer":"We also need images of the earth's surface","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/51.mp3"},{"answer":"which we can produce by means of computer-generation technology","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/52.mp3"},{"answer":"or with the help of satellite relays.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/53.mp3"},{"answer":"We've come a very long way from the early exploration of the world by sailing ships","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/54.mp3"},{"answer":"when geographers only had pens and paper at their disposal.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/55.mp3"},{"answer":"After we've gathered our information, we must analyse it!","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/56.mp3"},{"answer":"We need to look for patterns, most commonly those of causes and consequences.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/57.mp3"},{"answer":"This kind of information helps us to predict and resolve problems that could affect the world we live in.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/58.mp3"},{"answer":"But we don't keep all this information confidential.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/59.mp3"},{"answer":"We then need to publish our findings so that other people can access it and be informed by it.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/60.mp3"},{"answer":"And one way which this information can be published is in the form of maps.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/61.mp3"},{"answer":"You'll all have used one at some stage of your life already.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/62.mp3"},{"answer":"Let's consider the benefits of maps from a geographer's perspective.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/63.mp3"},{"answer":"Maps can be folded and put in a pocket","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/64.mp3"},{"answer":"and can provide a great store of reference when they're collected into an atlas.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/65.mp3"},{"answer":"They can depict the physical features of the entire planet if necessary,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/66.mp3"},{"answer":"or just a small part of it in much greater detail.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/67.mp3"},{"answer":"But there is a drawback.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/68.mp3"},{"answer":"You can't exactly replicate something that is three-dimensional, like our planet, on a flat piece of paper,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/69.mp3"},{"answer":"because paper has only two dimensions,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/70.mp3"},{"answer":"and that means there'll always be a certain degree of distortion on a map.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/71.mp3"},{"answer":"It can't be avoided.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/72.mp3"},{"answer":"We can also use aerial photographs...","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/73.mp3"},{"answer":"pictures taken by cameras at high altitude above the earth.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/74.mp3"},{"answer":"These are great for showing all kinds of geographical features that are not easy to see from the ground.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/75.mp3"},{"answer":"You can easily illustrate areas of diseased trees or how much traffic is on the road at a given time","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/76.mp3"},{"answer":"or information about deep sea beds, for example.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/77.mp3"},{"answer":"Then there are Landsats.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/78.mp3"},{"answer":"These are satellites that circle the earth","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/79.mp3"},{"answer":"and transmit visual information to computers at receiving stations.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/80.mp3"},{"answer":"They circle the earth several times a day","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/81.mp3"},{"answer":"and can provide a mass of information -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/82.mp3"},{"answer":"you'll all be familiar with the information they give us about the weather, for example.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/83.mp3"},{"answer":"So, what we're going to do now is look at a short presentation...","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-8-test-1-part-4-2023-07-24-23-14-14/84.mp3"}]
